// REJECTS: no viable alternative at input 'ExternalFormat#{'
//
// A Data element carries AT MOST ONE bare embedded-data body:
// `dataElement: ... { embeddedData? (dataResolver (dataResolver)*)? }`. Anything beyond the
// first must be a resolver -- `store::path: <embeddedData>;` -- with a target and a
// semicolon.
//
// The `?` is easy to read as `*`, and the two forms look nearly identical in a real file.
// A rewrite that accepts a list here builds a Data element with a second payload that
// legend-engine's protocol has no field for.
###Data
Data fixture::neg::TwoEmbeddedBodies
{
   ExternalFormat
   #{
      contentType: 'application/json';
      data: '{}';
   }#
   ExternalFormat
   #{
      contentType: 'application/xml';
      data: '<a/>';
   }#
}
